@@ -250,6 +250,15 @@
 
 ## SSL versions
 
+With OpenSSL 1.1.0 or newer, all protocol selectors use TLS version
+negotiation. The legacy values `2` and `3`, including `HTTPS_VERSION`, do
+not force SSLv2 or SSLv3. With older OpenSSL, the legacy methods are used
+when available, with version negotiation replacing an unavailable SSLv3
+method. The protocols enabled by the linked OpenSSL library and its
+configuration determine which connections can succeed.
+
+The following fallback order describes builds with older OpenSSL:
+
 `Crypt::SSLeay` tries very hard to connect to *any* SSL web server accomodating servers that are buggy, old or simply not standards-compliant.  To this effect, this module will try SSL connections in this order:
 
 *   SSL v23 : should allow v2 and v3 servers to pick their best type
