 =head1 SSL versions
 
+With OpenSSL 1.1.0 or newer, all protocol selectors use TLS version
+negotiation. The legacy values C<2> and C<3>, including C<HTTPS_VERSION>,
+do not force SSLv2 or SSLv3. With older OpenSSL, the legacy methods are
+used when available, with version negotiation replacing an unavailable
+SSLv3 method. The protocols enabled by the linked OpenSSL library and its
+configuration determine which connections can succeed.
+
+The following fallback order describes builds with older OpenSSL:
+
 C<Crypt::SSLeay> tries very hard to connect to I<any> SSL web server
 accommodating servers that are buggy, old or simply not standards-compliant.
 To this effect, this module will try SSL connections in this order:
